  "title": "The spin structure by computation",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Exact computation confirming ticket A and extending it to non-planar glue. (1) On every three-fold space with at most 22 points (the Fano space, the 13-point space, the four 19-point classes, and the 21- and 22-point spaces), on all or a stated number of minimal maps: every face has length 2 mod 4, every vertex lies on three distinct faces, the knot's spin structure has Arf invariant 0, the form vanishes on every difference of perfect matchings, and these differences realize exactly 3^h homology classes for h Fano atoms, the spin structures even on every handle. (2) On minimal maps of the 35-point space with non-planar (trisum) glue and the 43-point twisted cube: faces of length 2 mod 4, three distinct faces at every vertex, Arf invariant 0, and the form vanishing on sampled matching differences. (3) Four trisums of prisms (non-planar glue braces) are rigid of genus one, and on all of their minimal maps their Pfaffian signing is Kasteleyn with three distinct faces at every vertex, Arf invariant 0, and the matching differences fill the three even classes. (4) On the Heawood torus the four Kasteleyn classes have determinants of absolute value 24, 8, 8, 8; only the knot's class counts the 24 perfect matchings; the Cimasoni-Reshetikhin formula recovers 24 from the four. (5) On non-minimal maps the same signs can be Kasteleyn with an odd spin structure: on 1,500 seeded random maps each, 22 of 1,002 Kasteleyn maps of the 13-point space (genus 6 and 7) and 8 of 1,149 of the trisum (2,2,3) (genus 5) are odd; none of 1,240 Kasteleyn maps of the Heawood graph (genus 1 to 4); none below genus 3.",
